course: dictionary
lesson: 1062
title: Bottlenose dolphins
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bottlenose is a dolphin with a short, rounded snout shaped a bit like the neck of a bottle. You can see the two parts of the word, bottle and nose, and a picture in your head helps you remember it.
explain: «Each bottlenose dolphin has its own signature whistle that works like a name.» Here bottlenose describes the dolphin, so it works as an adjective. Ask yourself: which dolphin? The bottlenose one.
explain: The same word can also be a noun. «The bottlenoses leapt high out of the waves.» Here bottlenoses are the animals themselves, so you can count them. Check the words around the word to see which job it does.
fact: A bottlenose dolphin is a common grey dolphin with a short, bottle-shaped snout.
fact: A bottlenose whale is a kind of whale that dives very deep.
fact: Bottlenose dolphins are clever mammals that use echolocation and whistle to each other.
fact: They live in groups called pods, so a pod of bottlenoses is a group of them.
fact: «The Black Sea has three kinds of dolphin»: the harbour porpoise has a blunt face, not a beak, so it is not a dolphin with a snout like a bottle.
exercise: In «The Black Sea has three kinds: the bottlenose dolphin, the common dolphin and the harbour porpoise», what is a bottlenose dolphin? | A bird that dives for food | *A common grey dolphin with a short, bottle-shaped snout | A kind of seaweed | A small fish that lives in coral reefs
exercise: «Dolphins remember old friends' whistles for at least 20 years.» What does this tell you? | They cannot hear other dolphins | They forget their friends after one day | They can only whistle at night | *They can remember a friend's whistle for a very long time
exercise: Groups of dolphins live together in a pod. What is a pod? | A deep dive to the bottom of the sea | A single fin | *A group of dolphins living together | A kind of whistle
test: What does echolocation help dolphins do? | Fly over the waves | Change their colour | *Find things using sound echoes | Taste their food
test: What is a bottlenose whale? | *A kind of whale that dives very deep | A bird that hunts near cliffs | A snake that swims in the sea | A small fish that lives on coral
exam: Which sentence uses bottlenose as an adjective, describing a noun? | «The bottlenoses leapt high out of the waves.» | «A pod of bottlenoses swam past the boat.» | *«Each bottlenose dolphin has its own signature whistle.» | «Bottlenose is a long word to spell.»
